## Original Content
President Donald Trump had the White House's East Wing demolished in 2025 to make way for his controversial planned ballroom.

## Summary
The U.S. Supreme Court has allowed President Donald Trump to continue construction of his planned White House ballroom for the time being. The project involved the demolition of the White House's East Wing in 2025 and has been controversial.

## Key Points
- The Supreme Court issued a ruling permitting the White House ballroom construction to proceed for now
- President Donald Trump had the White House East Wing demolished in 2025 to make way for the ballroom
- The ballroom project has been described as controversial
- The ruling is temporary ('for now'), suggesting ongoing legal proceedings or challenges


